# TaskFlow – Task Management System 

## Project Overview 

TaskFlow is a web-based task management application designed to help users organize their daily activities, manage deadlines, and track their progress in one place. 

Users can create and manage tasks, assign priorities, set deadlines, and organize their tasks into categories such as Study, Personal, and Work. 

## Main Features 

### 1. User Authentication 

- Register a new account. 

- Login and logout. 

- Each user has their own private tasks. 

### 2. Main Dashboard 

The dashboard provides a quick overview of the user’s tasks and activities. It includes: 

- The three nearest upcoming incomplete tasks, sorted by deadline. 

- Three category cards: Study, Personal, and Work. 

- Each category card displays the number of tasks and opens its corresponding task list when clicked. 

- An Add New Task button for quickly creating tasks. 

- A Show All Tasks button to view all tasks. 

### 3. Task Management 

Users can: 

- Create new tasks. 

- View all their tasks. 

- Edit existing tasks. 

- Delete tasks. 

- Mark tasks as completed. 

- Set task deadlines. 

- Assign priorities: Low, Medium, and High. 

- Set task status: Pending, In Progress, and Completed. 

Marking a task as completed sets its status to Completed. Completed status and 'completed' are the same thing, not two separate fields.

Each task contains a title, description, category, priority, status, deadline, and creation date. 

### 4. Categories 

Tasks are organized into three main categories: 

The three categories (Study, Personal, Work) are fixed and the same for all users. Users cannot create their own categories.

   - Study: Assignments, exams, lectures, and university activities. 

- Personal: Personal activities, errands, and daily responsibilities. 

- • Work: Job-related tasks and professional activities. 

- Clicking a category displays only the tasks belonging to it. 

### 5. Search, Filtering, and Sorting 

- Filter tasks by priority. 

- Filter tasks by status. 

- Filter tasks by category. 

- Sort tasks by deadline (earliest or latest). 

- Search tasks by a keyword in the title (required feature).

### 6. Calendar View 

- Display tasks according to their deadlines. 

- Navigate between months. 

- Select a date to view its scheduled tasks. 

- Open task details from the calendar. 

### 7. Profile 

- View and update personal information. 

- Edit name and email (email must stay unique). 

- Change password. 

## Main Application Pages 

1. Login 2. Register 3. Dashboard 4. All Tasks 5. Category Tasks 6. Calendar 7. Profile 

Task creation and editing will be handled through reusable forms or pop-up windows (modals). 

## Suggested Technologies 

Python Flask + SQLite 

- Frontend: HTML, CSS, JavaScript 

- Backend: Python Flask 

- • Database: SQLite 

#### Why this stack: 

- Lightweight Python backend. 

- • Very little configuration. 

- SQLite doesn’t require a separate database server. 

- Good if you prefer Python. 

## Project Objective 

The main objective is to provide a simple, organized, and user-friendly platform that helps individuals manage their responsibilities, prioritize tasks, meet deadlines, and monitor their productivity. 

The project will demonstrate important Software Engineering concepts, including requirements analysis, system design, database management, user authentication, CRUD operations, and software testing. 
